{"step_index":162,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:32:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-29T20:02:55+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-29T20:02:55+05:30\nShowing lines 1-50 of 289\n1: # 🔍 FraudLens AI\n2: ### *Detect smarter. Explain every alert. Reduce false alarms.*\n3: \n4: > **Zeckathon PS2 — Explainable Financial Risk & Fraud Analytics**\n5: \n6: FraudLens AI is a complete, locally-runnable prototype that combines a genuine ML prediction pipeline, three-outcome triage, interactive graph analysis, chronological replay, and a full investigator workflow — all built without paid APIs or bank credentials.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## ✅ Quick Start (Windows / VS Code)\n11: \n12: ### Prerequisites\n13: - Python 3.12 ([download](https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3120/))\n14: - Node.js 20+ with npm ([download](https://nodejs.org/))\n15: \n16: ### Step 1 — Clone / Open the Project\n17: \n18: ```powershell\n19: # Open a new PowerShell terminal in VS Code\n20: cd \"C:\\path\\to\\fraudlens-ai\"\n21: ```\n22: \n23: ### Step 2 — Backend Setup\n24: \n25: ```powershell\n26: # Install Python dependencies\n27: pip install -r requirements.txt\n28: \n29: # Start the backend API server (from project root)\n30: cd backend\n31: python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload\n32: ```\n33: \n34: Backend will be available at: http://127.0.0.1:8000  \n35: Swagger API docs at: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs\n36: \n37: ### Step 3 — Frontend (Development Mode)\n38: \n39: Open a second terminal:\n40: \n41: ```powershell\n42: cd frontend\n43: npm install\n44: npm run dev\n45: ```\n46: \n47: Frontend will be available at: http://localhost:5173\n48: \n49: ### Step 4 — Frontend (Production Build — Served by Backend)\n50: "}
{"step_index":163,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:32:55Z","input_tokens":2849,"cache_read_tokens":107509,"output_tokens":386,"tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\S Nandhakumar\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\fraudlens-ai\\\\README.md\"","Replacement":"\"---\\n\\n## 🚀 Deploying to Vercel\\n\\nFraudLens AI is pre-configured for **1-click unified Vercel deployment** hosting both the React/TypeScript frontend (via edge CDN) and the Python FastAPI prediction engine (via Vercel Serverless Functions).\\n\\n### Method 1: Git Integration (Recommended — Zero Setup)\\n\\n1. Push this directory to your GitHub / GitLab repository.\\n2. Go to [vercel.com/new](https://vercel.com/new).\\n3. Import your repository.\\n4. Leave all build settings at default (`vercel.json` and root `package.json` automatically configure build, output directory, and serverless runtime).\\n5. Click **Deploy**.\\n\\nVercel will build the frontend into `frontend/dist` and mount the Python FastAPI backend on `/api/*` automatically!\\n\\n### Method 2: Vercel CLI\\n\\n```bash\\n# Install Vercel CLI if not already installed\\nnpm i -g vercel\\n\\n# From the fraudlens-ai project root:\\nvercel\\n```\\n\\nFollow the prompts:\\n- Set up and deploy? **Y**\\n- Which scope? **Select your account**\\n- Link to existing project? **N**\\n- Project name: **fraudlens-ai**\\n- Directory: **./**\\n- Want to modify settings? **N** (settings are pre-configured in `vercel.json`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📁 Project Structure\"","Target":"\"---\\n\\n## 📁 Project Structure\""}}]}
